# Frontend Standards

## Stack

Bootstrap 4/5 + jQuery + `$.ajax()` — no React/Vue/npm/webpack unless explicitly requested.

## Forms

```html
<div class="mb-3">
  <label for="email" class="form-label">Email Address</label>
  <input type="email" class="form-control" id="email" name="email" required>
  <?php echo form_error('email', '<div class="invalid-feedback d-block">', '</div>'); ?>
</div>
```

Every input needs `<label>` or `aria-label`. Meaningful `alt` on images (empty `alt=""` for decorative).

## AJAX Rules

- Global `$.ajaxSetup()` once in base layout (401 → login redirect)
- Always: `beforeSend` (disable btn/loader), `complete` (re-enable), `error` callback
- Check `response.status === 'success'` before processing data
- Use toastr/Bootstrap alerts, never raw `alert()`

## Event Delegation

```js
$(document).on('click', '.btn-edit', function() {
    editRecord($(this).data('id'));
});
```

## CSS Naming

- PHP: snake_case | JS: camelCase | CSS: kebab-case | Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Prefer Bootstrap utility classes over inline styles
- Mobile-first responsive (`d-none d-lg-block`, etc.)

## CDN Versions

Pin exactly (e.g. `bootstrap@5.3.2`, `jquery@3.7.1`) — never `@latest`. Track in PROJECT_MAP.md.

## Asset Layout

```
assets/css/   — module stylesheets
assets/js/    — app.js (global), module-specific JS
```

Load app JS in footer after CDN libraries (especially DataTables).

## Accessibility

4.5:1 contrast minimum. Keyboard-navigable interactive elements. No div-as-button without `role="button"` + `tabindex="0"`.
